# Delegation model policy

Subagents inherit the current chat or session model. Omit the delegation tool's
`model` argument by default; do not select a model from a role, provider, family,
reasoning tier, availability list, or an older configuration.

Use a model override only when the human user explicitly chooses it for the
current invocation. Record a persistent override only when the user explicitly
requests persistence and its scope. Never substitute a different model silently.

Independent review comes from separate evidence gathering and distinct review
focus, not a required change of model. Keep the useful worker and reviewer roles.
